            <div xml:id="d321">

                <pb facs="0312" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9106: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-31T10:00:00+08:00">July 31, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 31—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. City quiet today. Some firing during the night as Japanese cleared out some
                    remnants of <hi rendition="#italic">Paoantui</hi> or other hostile Chinese from
                    the Chinese city. Japanese yesterday afternoon completed destruction of Nankai
                    University by artillery fire, air bombing and burning, and bombarded several
                    buildings in the Chinese City, particularly Nankai middle school and girls
                    school.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
